title: Munich Is Not Alone
subtitle: If the rest of the Reich moves, Noske cannot spare his regiments.
view-if: crisis_bavaria = 1 and bav_solidarity_done = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; bav_solidarity_done = 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= Munich Is Not Alone

In the Ruhr the miners are striking for the six-hour shift. Saxony is restless. If the rest of the Reich moved now, Noske would have to keep at home the regiments he means for Bavaria. But the party is banned in half of Germany, and its paper is printed in cellars.

- @strike: Call a strike across the Reich for Munich.
- @volunteers: Send volunteers from Saxony and Thuringia.

@strike
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Von Oven will be a week late. Every district that comes out will be policed for it.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids a political mass strike of this kind.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.bav_solidarity = 1;
Q.e19_bav_whites += 7;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.startStrike('ruhr');
RG.startStrike('saxony');
RG.district('ruhr', {repression: 6});
RG.district('saxony', {repression: 6});
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Von Oven\'s army: ' + Q.e19_bav_whites + ' days from Munich';
!}

The call goes out from the illegal Zentrale. In the Ruhr and in Saxony, hundreds of thousands come out.

@volunteers
subtitle: A few hundred reliable comrades for the Red Army.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_bav_army += 2;
Q.e19_bav_trained = 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.district('saxony', {members: -0.03});
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e19_bav_army + ',000 men';
!}

Small groups cross the Thuringian Forest on foot and by goods train. Some are arrested at Hof. The rest reach Munich with rifles in their luggage.
